- Refresh pipeline preset selectors in-place when the preset inventory changes, preserving in-progress stage edits.
- Always dispatch `audioRecorderPresetsChanged` after saving the in-memory preset list, even when `localStorage` persistence throws.
- Harden the Windows portable build against transient Electron download failures by retrying dependency installation, caching Electron runtime downloads, and reusing the installed Electron runtime for packaging.
- Add Cypress coverage for the reported stale selector path and archive the issue/PR/CI/local evidence under `docs/case-studies/issue-143/`.

Fixes Jhon-Crow/audio-recorder-with-visualization#143

## Root Cause
The remaining UI failure was in `savePresets()`: the preset-change event was dispatched inside the same `try` block as `localStorage.setItem()`. If browser storage threw, for example under quota pressure from large preset payloads, the preset could still exist in memory and render in the preset sidebar, but pipeline stage selectors never received the refresh event and stayed on `No saved visualization presets`.

The later CI failures were separate infrastructure failures: Electron `33.4.11` downloads returned HTTP 504, first during `electron-builder` packaging and then during the `electron` package `install.js` step inside `npm ci`.

## Tests
- `npm run typecheck`
- `npm run lint`
- `npm test -- --runInBand` - 9 suites / 341 tests passed
- `npm run build` - passed with existing Rollup warnings
- `CYPRESS_baseUrl=http://localhost:8080 npx cypress run --spec cypress/e2e/pipeline-mode.cy.js --config video=false` - 22 tests passed after merging `upstream/main`
- Playwright browser verification with preset persistence forced to throw; the first stage selector contained `Pipeline Memory Preset`.
- GitHub Actions `Build Portable EXE` run `27123260069` passed on commit `5babe5d`, including tests, library build, portable EXE packaging, and artifact upload.

